.TH TERMSNAP-DEMO 1 "2026-01-01" "termsnap tests" "Test Manual"
.SH NAME
termsnap-demo \- a page that exists only to be read in a pager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B termsnap-demo
[\fB\-\-width\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] \fIfile\fR...
.SH DESCRIPTION
This page is long enough to need scrolling: the first screen shows only the
beginning, and the rest is reached with Page Down or Space.
.PP
The pager shows bold and underlined words with terminal attributes, so the
screenshot keeps them as styles rather than as backspace sequences.
.PP
Every paragraph below repeats the same idea in different words, to make the
page longer than a screen of thirty lines without adding anything to remember.
.PP
Paragraph one. The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog, and then jumps
back again to check that the dog is still lazy.
.PP
Paragraph two. Pack my box with five dozen liquor jugs, said the fox, and the
dog did not move.
.PP
Paragraph three. How vexingly quick daft zebras jump, thought the fox, who had
never seen a zebra.
.PP
Paragraph four. Sphinx of black quartz, judge my vow, and the pager scrolled
quietly to the next screen.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-width " N"
Wrap lines at \fIN\fR columns.
.TP
.B \-\-color
Use colour in the output.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
termsnap-demo --width 60 README
termsnap-demo --color *.txt
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR less (1),
.BR man (1)
.PP
The word needle appears once, here, so that a search lands on this line.
